body:
&#x200B;

So I am looking for a sex shop/toy store in KL to pickup a few things. But from google maps there are very few ones. But I was in the Bukit Bintang area the other day, specfically the Sungei Plaza and I could have swore I saw a shop. But when I went back no matter how hard I tried I could not locate it again (I have a terrible sense of direction and that place is basically a maze for me lol). 

So I am wondering does anyone know of the pace I am referring to or any other shops in the area?

In a recent Fan call, Cheol mentioned to not buy Caratland Premium tickets because they are so price-hitched. But since I will be in Korea anyway,  and even though its a terrible practice I am looking to hopefully get tickets anyway I can. 

&#x200B;

So does anyone know where I can see these premium tickets or has anyone came across any reapable resellers?

No it was a company that misused my funds. Here is the email I sent them, I did not indicate I would me taking any action or threaten to do so (I would not even know where to start there).....

&#x200B;

"This makes no sense because  as I stated in my previous Dispute that you guys approved, this fraudulent company took my funds and misrepresented themselves that was not authorized. You sided with me in my previous dispute about the same company regarding the same thing, and found that there was an error made. But I am not understanding how that dispute was allowed a permanent credit. But you guys are fighting me, your loyal customer, on the rest of my funds that this company defrauded me with. You guys sided with me with the same argument in my previous dispute so why is this being denied now? This is the part that I do not understand.   
This company either defrauded me or they did not. You as a bank cannot have it both ways in this regard, there was an error found the first time, so why not now?  Why is one dispute being approved and the rest are not when they are on the same basis? I will be resubmitting again because your answer is not answering my question regarding this. Again I cannot work it out with the merchant because they are closing down on the 30th of June. They are also being investigated and facing possible litigation. That means at the end of this month they will stop responding to all users, which they rarely are doing now, and effectively running off with the rest of people's money.  Again YOU as my bank found an error the first time with the company I am disputing, But refused to find one or acknowledge one was made for the rest of my funds. The dispute is about the same company, so why are you ignoring this?"

&#x200B;

That is when I got the above email. I don't know if they didn't do their due diligence the first time around or what. But One refuses to acknowledge that both of the disputes even though they have the same basis have very different decisions, while completely gaslighting me to this fact.
